{
  "id": "25726_kowagaraseru",
  "headword": "{怖|こわ}がらせる",
  "reading": "こわがらせる",
  "romaji": "kowagaraseru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to frighten; to scare",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to frighten; to scare; to intimidate",
      "explanation": "To cause someone to feel fear or anxiety. The causative form of 怖がる, meaning to make someone afraid."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "25726_kowagaraseru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{子|こ}どもを{怖|こわ}がらせないで。",
      "english": "Don't scare the children.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25726_kowagaraseru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{暗|くら}い{話|はなし}で{友達|ともだち}を{怖|こわ}がらせた。",
      "english": "I scared my friend with a dark story.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25726_kowagaraseru_ex3",
      "japanese": "わざと{大|おお}きな{声|こえ}を{出|だ}して{弟|おとうと}を{怖|こわ}がらせるのはやめなさい。",
      "english": "Stop deliberately scaring your little brother by making loud noises.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A causative form of {怖|こわ}がる (to be scared). While {怖|こわ}がる describes someone feeling fear, {怖|こわ}がらせる means to cause that fear in another person. Often used when describing pranks, intimidation, or unintentional frightening.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {子|こ}どもを{怖|こわ}がらせる: to scare a child\n- {人|ひと}を{怖|こわ}がらせる: to frighten someone\n- わざと{怖|こわ}がらせる: to scare on purpose\n- {脅|おど}して{怖|こわ}がらせる: to threaten and frighten\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {脅|おど}かす: to startle or threaten — focuses on the sudden, shocking action rather than the resulting fear\n- {怯|おび}えさせる: to terrify — stronger, implies deep or lasting fear\n- {驚|おどろ}かす: to surprise — neutral; not necessarily negative, can be a pleasant surprise",
